   196	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   197	    """
   198	    Turn each edge-touching drill segment into a material-budget tunnel through same-color solid blocks.
   199	
   200	    Input structure:
   201	    - The background is the most common color.
   202	    - One foreground color forms separated solid rectangular blocks, and the other foreground
   203	      color forms straight one-cell-thick drill segments.
   204	    - Each drill segment touches exactly one block edge perpendicularly, and later blocks may
   205	      lie farther along the same row or column.
   206	
   207	    Rule:
   208	    - Erase all drill segments.
   209	    - For a segment of length L, start at the touched block cell and move straight inward;
   210	      block cells cost one unit and are erased, while background cells cost nothing.
   211	    - If the Lth paid cell is reached, paint that cell with the drill color; if all material
   212	      on the ray is drilled with budget left over, paint the first background cell after the
   213	      final block instead.
